Bound the separable FIR intermediate without changing the convolution.

Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-08.
Vulkan previews/exports above 16 MiB retain the full input and output but
store vertical results in at most 8 MiB (or one row). Horizontal filtering
needs only that same row; reflection uses the original canvas, and both
float32 passes keep their tap/accumulation order. The consuming path keeps
its existing two-plane reuse. Small live previews keep the two dispatches.
An exact-capacity pooled allocation prevents a small band from borrowing
an idle full-frame buffer. Bounded blocks only serve equal-sized requests,
so later small constants cannot retain them. This is not a full-pipeline
streaming executor.

